{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And Egypt — not spirit.</b> An angel, like ורוחו (and His spirit) (Isaiah 48:16)." "<b>His hand.</b> His blow." "<b>Together.</b> Egypt and those who flee to them. For the meaning is that the king of Assyria destroyed Egypt when he came to Jerusalem." "<b>Shall cease.</b> Complete, like יחסיון (they are ended) (Psalms 36:8)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:10.603653143Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}